    "source": "\n**Frame:** Back in the dated creator frame, `4 SEPTEMBER`. Curt has the book's familiar incident timeline on the desk, the one the reader has been following since [page 016](016.md). He draws a second horizontal lane beneath it and labels it `PUBLIC WIKI`. The upper lane keeps its label: `ARTIFACTORY`.\n\n**Action:** The calendar the book presented as complete acquires a lane.\n\n**Caption:**\n> THE BOOK DREW ONE LANE BECAUSE ONE LANE WAS PUBLIC.\n\n**Provenance:** `reconstructed` — creator action; the retrospective calendar is the project's construction from two sourced records.\n\n",
    "title": "The creator adds a second timeline lane"
